# SQL's `left` as a join kind: DS0123 with a fix to `leftouter`.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | join kind = left 'customers.csv' on customerId
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..67
  PIPELINE@0..66
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    JOIN_OP@20..66
      IDENT@20..24 "join"
      WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
      JOIN_KIND@25..36
        IDENT@25..29 "kind"
        WHITESPACE@29..30 " "
        EQ@30..31 "="
        WHITESPACE@31..32 " "
        IDENT@32..36 "left"
      WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
      LITERAL@37..52
        STRING@37..52 "'customers.csv'"
      WHITESPACE@52..53 " "
      IDENT@53..55 "on"
      WHITESPACE@55..56 " "
      NAME_REF@56..66
        IDENT@56..66 "customerId"
  WHITESPACE@66..67 "\n"

error[DS0123]: unknown join kind `left`
  --> query:1:33
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | join kind = left 'customers.csv' on customerId
  |                                 ^^^^ not a join kind
  |
  = help: write `kind = leftouter`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | join kind = leftouter 'customers.csv' on customerId
which parses without errors
